4.3. The Withdrawal. A withdrawal (formally, W ) is a tuple of data describing a consensus layer validator's withdrawal of some amount of its staked Ether. A withdrawal is created and validated in the consensus layer of the blockchain and then pushed to the execution layer. A withdrawal is composed of the following fields:

globalIndex: zero based incrementing withdrawal index that acts as a unique identifier for this withdrawal; formally W g .

validatorIndex: index of consensus layer's validator this withdrawal corresponds to; formally W v . recipient: the 20-byte address that will receives Ether from this withdrawal; formally W r .

amount: a nonzero amount of Ether denominated in Gwei (10 9 Wei); formally W a .

