It is  pointless to implement a  stability test  in  a system  in  which Byzantine failures are possible and  a processor  or  message can be  delayed for an  arbitrary length of  time without being considered faulty. This is because  no  deterministic protocol can  implement agreement under these  conditions [Fischer et  al.  851.' Since it  is  impossible to satisfy the  Agreement requirement, there is no  point in satisfying the Order require-

